say $double(5); # 10 the variable `$double` holds the subroutine, and `$double(5)` calls it with the argument `5`. pointy blocks raku offers a shorter notation for the same thing — the _pointy block_. it uses the arrow `->` to introduce the parameters, and needs neither the word `sub` nor parentheses around them: my $double = -> $x {
