supplies defined outside every `whenever` so far has created its supply right there in the header — `whenever supply.from-list(...)`. that reads well for a quick example, but real programs rarely have their event source on hand at exactly that spot. more often a supply is built somewhere else — returned by a function, produced by a `supplier`, or handed to you by a socket or a timer — and arrives as a plain variable. a `whenever` is just as happy to watch a named supply: my $sensors  = supply.from-list(18, 21, 19);
my $messages = supply.from-list('hi', 'bye');

react {
    whenever $sensors {
        say "temperature: $_";
